["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Deer hunters fight the nose. Goose hunters fight the eyes. Every flock you lose at 80 m saw something.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of goose senses. Eyes, the longest bar: they see fine detail 2.5 to 3 times farther than you, 80 percent. Ears, a middle bar: best at 1 to 4 kilohertz, the range of a human voice, 80 percent. Nose, a short bar: weak and used for food, not for hunters, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A goose lives through its eyes</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Eyes</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"55\" width=\"300\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Detail 2.5 to 3 times farther than you (80%)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"157\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ears</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"133\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Best at 1 to 4 kHz, like your voice (80%)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nose</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"211\" width=\"60\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weak; used for food, not hunters (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sight first, hearing second, smell a distant third <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Beat the eyes and you beat most geese (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Eyes: field of view, colour, detail, motion, low light.</li><li>Ears: what they hear best.</li><li>Nose: what is known, and what is lore.</li><li>How a flock combines them: the watchers.</li><li>How to beat each sense, in one table.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a goose head and its field of view. A wide orange area covers almost all the way around: wide side views on both sides. A narrow grey blind spot sits behind the head. A darker wedge in front is seen with both eyes, wide enough to see its own bill tip. The goose sees ground and sky at once. All 90 percent, from studies of Canada goose eyes, which give no degree values in the summary.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 170 L90 250 A140 140 0 1 1 310 250 Z\" fill=\"#fde3cf\"/><path d=\"M200 170 L90 250 L310 250 Z\" fill=\"#cfcfcf\"/><path d=\"M200 170 L165 65 L235 65 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".55\"/><g transform=\"translate(200 170)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-6 -20 L0 -40 L6 -20Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both eyes: sees its bill tip (90%)</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wide side</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">view (90%)</text><text x=\"350\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wide side</text><text x=\"350\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">view (90%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Narrow blind spot behind (90%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sees ground and sky at once (90%)</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What a goose sees (head from above)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Almost all the way around, with a narrow blind spot behind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>They see ground and sky at once <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what the eye studies found</summary><ul><li>Canada geese have narrow blind areas, wide side vision, wide binocular fields and can see their own bill tips (90%, Fernandez Juricic and others 2011).</li><li>Their sharpest retina band runs at a slant (oblique), not flat. It lets a goose scan the ground and the sky at the same time, or line up with the horizon by tilting its head <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Because of this they move their heads less than many birds while watching in open fields <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. More head movement in cluttered cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>The study summary gives no degree values. Do not trust a number you see quoted without a source. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>What it means: there is almost no \"behind\" to hide in on open ground. Hide under cover, not just out of the line of sight (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A colour spectrum from 380 to 700 nanometres with four goose cone peaks at 409 violet, 458 blue, 509 green and 580 orange, 90 percent. People have 3 cone types. Shiny faces, guns and new fabric stand out, a Tip. Waterfowl see from near ultraviolet to red, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Colour: 4 cone types, you have 3</text><defs><linearGradient id=\"mgs-colour-cones-g\" x1=\"0\" x2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#7b2cbf\"/><stop offset=\".2\" stop-color=\"#3a0ca3\"/><stop offset=\".4\" stop-color=\"#4a7fb0\"/><stop offset=\".55\" stop-color=\"#2e7d32\"/><stop offset=\".72\" stop-color=\"#f9c74f\"/><stop offset=\".85\" stop-color=\"#e8590c\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#c0392b\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect x=\"30\" y=\"180\" width=\"340\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"url(#mgs-colour-cones-g)\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">380 nm</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">700 nm</text><path d=\"M21 175 Q61 40 101 175\" fill=\"#7b2cbf\" opacity=\".45\" stroke=\"#7b2cbf\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"60.8125\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">409</text><path d=\"M73 175 Q113 40 153 175\" fill=\"#3a0ca3\" opacity=\".45\" stroke=\"#3a0ca3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"112.875\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">458</text><path d=\"M127 175 Q167 40 207 175\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" opacity=\".45\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"167.0625\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">509</text><path d=\"M202 175 Q242 40 282 175\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".45\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"242.5\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">580</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Goose peaks: violet, blue, green, orange (90%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shiny faces, guns and new fabric pop out (Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Waterfowl see near UV to red (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>4 cone types; the shortest tuned to violet <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Fine detail 2.5 to 3 times farther than you <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the colour science</summary><ul><li>Canada geese have four visual pigments with peaks at 409, 458, 509 and 580 nm (90%, Moore and others 2012).</li><li>That is a violet sensitive system. Ducks Unlimited describes waterfowl colour vision as running from near ultraviolet to red <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The brightest patches to another goose are the cheek, crown, neck and upper tail: the marks they use to keep flocks together <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. That is why decoy heads and chinstraps matter (Tip).</li><li>Waterfowl see fine detail 2.5 to 3 times farther than people (80%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Side set eyes give weak depth sense. Birds move the head to judge distance <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>What it means: a bare face, a shiny gun, fresh blind fabric and frosted decoys all stand out (Tip, 65%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: three geese glide toward a hunter hidden in a layout blind in stubble. As they come close, the hunter lifts a pale face to look. The geese flare: they turn and climb away out of range. Final card: face down, hat brim low, until the shot call, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One face up, the whole flock flares</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9c48f\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"11\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"19\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"25\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"33\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"39\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"47\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"53\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"61\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"67\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"75\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"81\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"89\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"103\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"109\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"117\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"123\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"131\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"137\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"145\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"151\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"159\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"165\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"173\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"179\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"187\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"193\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"201\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"207\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"215\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"221\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"229\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"235\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"243\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"249\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"257\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"263\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"271\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"277\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"285\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"291\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"299\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"305\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"313\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"319\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"327\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"333\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"341\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"347\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"355\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"361\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"369\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"383\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"389\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"397\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"403\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(250 230) scale(1.6)\"><rect x=\"-22\" y=\"-8\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d9c48f\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"272\" cy=\"230\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#f2c9a0\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.2s\"/></circle><path id=\"mgs-face-flare-p\" d=\"M20 60 C 120 80, 180 140, 215 150 C 240 120, 260 70, 300 30 L 340 60\" fill=\"none\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g></g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.62;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-face-flare-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g><g transform=\"translate(-26 14)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g></g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.62;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-face-flare-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g><g transform=\"translate(-26 -14)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M16 -2 L36 -4 L36 1 L16 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M45 -3 L51 -1 L45 1Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-8 -3 L6 -30 L12 -3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-20 0 L-28 -3 L-28 3Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g></g><animateMotion dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\" keyPoints=\"0;0.62;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;1\"><mpath href=\"#mgs-face-flare-p\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"242\" width=\"190\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Face down, hat brim low</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">until the shot call (Tip)</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.4s\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Face up!</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>One face up, the whole flock flares. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Movement and glare flare more birds than anything <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Keep your face down until the shot call (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: motion rules from goose guides</summary><ul><li>Waterfowl flare at movement in the blind and at the glint of a gun barrel (80%, Ducks Unlimited senses article).</li><li>Frosted decoys glare at sunrise. Set decoys as late as you can without missing the first flight (65%, Ducks Unlimited goose guide).</li><li>Hide hands and face: face mask or paint, gloves, hat brim low (Tip).</li><li>Watch birds through the mesh or the brim, never by lifting your head (Tip).</li><li>One hunter calls the shot. Everyone moves at once, then not before (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Light</th><th>What a wintering flock did (80%, Raveling 1972)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Clear dawn</td><td>First birds 15 min before sunrise, main flight at or just after sunrise</td></tr><tr><td>Overcast dawn</td><td>About 15 min later</td></tr><tr><td>Clear dusk</td><td>Back between sunset and civil twilight</td></tr><tr><td>Cloudy dusk</td><td>Back before sunset</td></tr><tr><td>Full moon visible</td><td>Back later in the evening</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Geese fly by light levels: first birds about 15 minutes before sunrise in clear weather <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Cloud delays them about 15 minutes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: night and the moon</summary><ul><li>A Saskatchewan flock started its morning flight at about 32 foot candles of light (80%, quoted in Raveling and others 1972).</li><li>Barnacle geese in the Netherlands fed at night only around the full moon (75%, Wildfowl journal). For Canada geese night feeding under the moon is hunter report only (Tip).</li><li>Your legal shooting light starts half an hour before sunrise <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. The first geese often come about then (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-06\">Chapter 6</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A frequency bar from 0 to 10 kilohertz. Birds hear best from 1 to 4 kilohertz and little above 10, 80 percent. Truck doors, shell clinks and talking fall in the range they hear best: shut doors softly, whisper, keep shells quiet, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Goose ears: tuned to your voice range</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"120\" width=\"340\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#eee\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"64.0\" y=\"120\" width=\"102.0\" height=\"40\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"115.0\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Best 1 to 4 kHz</text><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"98.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"166.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"234.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"302.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"370.0\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">kilohertz (kHz)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Most birds hear little above 10 kHz (80%)</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"216\" width=\"340\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Truck doors, shell clinks, talking: all inside</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the range they hear best. Shut doors softly,</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">whisper, keep shells quiet (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most birds hear best at 1 to 4 kHz (kilohertz), the range of your voice <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>A slammed truck door is a goose alarm (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: hearing in full</summary><ul><li>Bird hearing in air is mostly below 10 kHz, best at 1 to 4 kHz (80%, sea duck hearing paper).</li><li>Diving ducks tested best at 1 to 3 kHz; lesser scaup best at 2 to 3 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. No goose audiogram found. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>Waterfowl ears have no outer flap; soft feathers cover the openings and cut wind noise (80%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Hearing keeps mates and families together in noisy flocks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Geese use about 13 calls (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>What it means: your call is heard. So are tailgates, zippers, shell boxes and talking (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view of a field spread with the wind blowing right to left. A goose comes from downwind, flies past the decoys, swings around upwind, turns back and glides down against the wind into the open landing hole beside the hide. Final label: into the wind, into the hole.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#d9c27a\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M360 30 L300 30 M309.0 25.7 L300 30 L309.0 34.3\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wind</text>\n  <path id=\"sb-goose-field-p\" d=\"M20 270 C 120 260, 380 240, 360 120 S 120 60, 70 150 S 140 200, 180 190\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(250 120)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(280 150)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(240 170)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(300 190)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(270 210)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(320 140)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(330 220)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M7 1 L13 5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(290 110)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M5 -2 L9 -14\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(240 220)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M5 -2 L9 -14\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n  <ellipse cx=\"180\" cy=\"186\" rx=\"40\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"226\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <text x=\"168\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hide</text>\n  <g><g transform=\"rotate(0)\"><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse rx=\"18\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-1\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M8 -3 Q2 -20.0 -10 -32.0 Q-8 -16.0 -8 -3Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M8 3 Q2 20.0 -10 32.0 Q-8 16.0 -8 3Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-16 0 L-26 -5 L-26 5Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/></g></g><animateMotion dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#sb-goose-field-p\"/></animateMotion></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.6s\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"52\" width=\"176\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Into the wind,</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">into the hole</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Wind matters for landing, not for scent. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Smell is weak in waterfowl; they rely on sight <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>No study found showing geese smell hunters (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what is known</summary><ul><li>Waterfowl smell is not as keen as a dog's, but they do detect odours (80%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Greylag geese can tell food plants from other plants by smell <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>About 400 taste buds in waterfowl versus about 9,000 in people <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter lore says scent control does not matter for geese (Tip). Wind still decides everything, because geese land into it. See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">Chapter 9</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a feeding flock. Birds on the edges hold their heads up and are circled orange: they are watching. Ganders and edge birds watch more, 75 percent. In a bigger flock each bird watches less, 70 percent. Many heads up means they are nervous, a Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Who is watching? Heads up at the edges</text><g transform=\"translate(150 155) rotate(36) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(229 96) rotate(9) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(184 197) rotate(14) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"197\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(244 140) rotate(10) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(106 157) rotate(33) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"157\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(93 196) rotate(16) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"99\" cy=\"196\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(304 140) rotate(-23) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"140\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(149 104) rotate(6) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(273 140) rotate(-28) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(228 187) rotate(-36) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"234\" cy=\"187\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(191 161) rotate(-23) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(310 99) rotate(23) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"316\" cy=\"99\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(128 191) rotate(-13) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"191\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(279 81) rotate(-7) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"81\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(261 179) rotate(15) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"13\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(106 100) rotate(40) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"100\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(100 118) rotate(-2) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"118\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(300 190) rotate(13) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse rx=\"9\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><line x1=\"7\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><circle cx=\"306\" cy=\"190\" r=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: heads up, watching</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ganders and edge birds watch more (75%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bigger flock: each bird watches less (70%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Many heads up = they are nervous (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Edge birds and ganders keep heads up more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Many heads up at once: they are nervous (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: vigilance studies</summary><ul><li>In pre nesting Canada geese, males were more vigilant than females and more so at the flock edge (75%, Wildfowl journal).</li><li>In white fronted geese, birds watched a road less as flock size grew <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Head up does not always mean alarm; some head up time is social <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A big feeding flock can feel safe and relaxed. A small group of wary birds is harder to fool (Tip).</li><li>Count heads up when you glass a field. Rising numbers mean leave them alone today (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>How to beat it (Tip unless shown)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Eyes, shape</td><td>Hide in or beside cover; brush the blind with field stubble</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes, motion</td><td>Face down, one shot caller, move together</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes, shine</td><td>Mud the blind, matte gun, face mask, late decoys on frost</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Quiet doors and gear, mouth call only (electronic calls banned, 99%)</td></tr><tr><td>Nose</td><td>Not the problem. Play the wind for landing</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why the call rule is in this table</summary><ul><li>Electronic calls and recordings are banned for migratory birds in BC (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book: migratory birds</a>). Mouth calls are fine (95%, my reading in the Rule Book).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"Eyes first, ears next, nose last: hide well, sit still, stay fast.\"</li><li>\"Face up, flock up.\"</li><li>\"Four cones beat your three: if it shines, they see.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>2.5 to 3</strong>. A goose sees detail 2.5 to 3 times as far as you <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>Hide first, decoys second, call last. Widely repeated by goose guides: concealment is the biggest single factor.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Fernandez Juricic 2011, Moore 2012, Raveling 1972, Ducks Unlimited senses article, hearing and vigilance studies. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/icwdm_usdanwrc/1291\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fernandez Juricic and others 2011, Brain Behavior and Evolution 77:147, abstract</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/icwdm_usdanwrc/1170\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Moore and others 2012, Journal of Experimental Biology 215:3442, abstract</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/understanding-waterfowl-the-five-senses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Understanding waterfowl: the five senses (J. Coluccy, 2017)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://archive.org/download/biostor-200086/biostor-200086.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Raveling, Crews and Klimstra 1972</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10658911/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sea duck hearing paper, PMC10658911</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildfowl.wwt.org.uk/index.php/wildfowl/article/view/692\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildfowl journal, lunar rhythm in barnacle geese</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wildfowl.wwt.org.uk/index.php/wildfowl/article/download/833/833\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildfowl journal, Canada goose vigilance</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/goose-hunting-tips-tactics/the-ultimate-guide-to-hunting-canada-geese\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited goose hunting guide</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.grandviewoutdoors.com/bird-hunting/waterfowl/12-tips-for-goose-hunters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grand View Outdoors, 12 tips for goose hunters</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-geese.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]